[0.001, "o", "=== findings (out/findings.md) ===\r\n"]
[0.010, "o", "# Findings — Novapump NP-200 SRS (synthetic)\r\n\r\n> **DRAFT — requires engineer review. Not for execution.** Findings are suggestions for the reviewing engineer.\r\n\r\n\r\n## High (4)\r\n\r\n### F-001 · orphan_trace · deterministic\r\n- **Cited:** NP-REQ-025\r\n- **Rationale:** NP-REQ-025 traces to NP-SYS-007, which does not exist in the system requirements.\r\n\r\n### F-002 · baseline_drift · deterministic\r\n- **Cited:** L-16\r\n- **Rationale:** L-16 (legacy) was changed after sign-off: \"20%\" -> \"25%\". Check that this went through change control.\r\n\r\n### F-003 · baseline_drift · deterministic\r\n- **Cited:** L-19\r\n- **Rationale:** L-19 (legacy) was changed after sign-off: removed \"and time\" after \"set the date\"; removed \"and time\" after \"Date\". Check that this went through change control.\r\n\r\n### F-004 · contradiction · llm\r\n- **Cited:** NP-REQ-009, NP-REQ-011\r\n- **Rationale:** NP-REQ-009 says \"limit a single bolus to a maximum of 10 U\" for the Pediatric profile, while NP-REQ-011 says to \"reject any bolus request above 15"]
[0.000, "o", " U\" for the same profile. The two give different maximum bolus values for the same profile.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Medium (3)\r\n\r\n### F-005 · untestable · deterministic\r\n- **Cited:** NP-REQ-018\r\n- **Rationale:** NP-REQ-018 is not measurable: \"The pump shall respond quickly to a press of the Bolus button.\"\r\n\r\n### F-006 · missing_requirement · llm\r\n- **Cited:** NP-REQ-014\r\n- **Rationale:** NP-REQ-014 states \"When Child Lock is ON, the pump shall disable the Bolus button\", but no requirement says how the pump responds when the user presses the disabled button, whether with feedback, a tone, or an explicit no response.\r\n\r\n### F-007 · incomplete_enumeration · llm\r\n- **Cited:** NP-REQ-001, NP-REQ-024\r\n- **Rationale:** NP-REQ-001 lists four delivery modes (Basal, Bolus, Extended Bolus, Suspend), while NP-REQ-024 lists only \"Basal, Bolus, and Suspend\" for Settings configuration. NP-REQ-024 applies to both profiles, and the Pediatric-only restriction in NP-REQ-010 does not explain omitting Extended Bolus for Adult.\r\n"]
[4.097, "o", "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
